\section{Conclusion and Future Work}
We present a formal method to quantify the simulation gap function between a mathematical model and a simulator. Our method enables the use of model-based control techniques to meet desired specifications. If the simulator closely resembles reality, incorporating the simulation gap function allows seamless controller deployment in the real world. Our future work will extend this approach to real-world.

