\paragraph{NDCG@20.} NDCG@20 evaluates the quality of ranking by assigning higher scores to relevant items that appear earlier in the top-20 list:
\begin{equation}
    \text{NDCG@20} = \frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}|} \sum_{u \in \mathcal{V}} \frac{1}{\text{IDCG}_u^{(20)}} \sum_{i=1}^{20} \frac{\mathbb{I}(r_{ui} \in \mathcal{G}_u)}{\log_2(i+1)},
\end{equation}

where $r_{ui}$ is the item at rank $i$ for agent $u$, $\mathcal{G}_u$ is the ground-truth relevant set, and $\text{IDCG}_u^{(20)}$ is the ideal DCG for agent $u$ (i.e., when all relevant items are ranked at the top).



