Complex mathematical reasoning remains a significant challenge for large language models \cite[LLMs;][]{ luo2024improve,li2023bert,10.1162/tacl_a_00594}.
Techniques like Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting~\cite{wei2022chain, kojima2022large, wang2022self} have improved LLM performance by encouraging the generation of intermediate reasoning steps.
However, CoT explanations are not always faithful to the actual reasoning process of the model~\cite{bentham2024chain, turpin2024language, yee2024dissociation}; with final answers that may not logically follow from the reasoning chain, suggesting that LLMs can fabricate reasoning paths~\cite{lyu2023faithful}.

