\title{\LARGE \bf Ground-Effect-Aware Modeling and Control for Multicopters}

\begin{document}
    \maketitle

\begin{abstract}





% 旋翼无人机上的地面效应引入了一些挑战，例如额外升力导致的控制误差，额外力矩导致的近地面飞行时可能出现的振荡，以及地面气流对空气阻力、混控矩阵等控制模型的影响。
% 本文通过各种手段，包括测力支架、真实飞行，采集了无人机近地飞行的动力学数据并加以分析，首次归纳出了地面效应作用在无人机上的力矩的数学模型。
% 也充分验证验证了地面效应对空气阻力、混控矩阵的影响。
The ground effect on multicopters introduces several challenges, such as control errors caused by additional lift, oscillations that may occur during near-ground flight due to external torques, and the influence of ground airflow on models such as the rotor drag and the mixing matrix.
This article collects and analyzes the dynamics data of near-ground multicopter flight through various methods, including force measurement platforms and real-world flights. For the first time, we summarize the mathematical model of the external torque of multicopters under ground effect.
The influence of ground airflow on rotor drag and the mixing matrix is also verified through adequate experimentation and analysis. Through simplification and derivation, the differential flatness of the multicopter's dynamic model under ground effect is confirmed.
% 为了消除这些扰动模型对控制的影响，我们提出了一种结合INDI和扰动模型的方法
% 该方法可以使得无人机在高空和低空的控制效果基本一致。
% 在该方法中，地面效应下的额外推力、rotor drag的变化都被考虑在内，并使用前馈模型进行补偿
% 地面效应的额外力矩可以等效为重心和转动惯量的变化，从而使得动力学模型中不存在回正力矩。
% 最终的实验显示，使用本文提出的方法，在降低了45.3%的控制误差（RMSE）。
To mitigate the influence of these disturbance models on control, we propose a control method that combines dynamic inverse and disturbance models, ensuring consistent control effectiveness at both high and low altitudes.
In this method, the additional thrust and variations in rotor drag under ground effect are both considered and compensated through feedforward models.
The leveling torque of ground effect can be equivalently represented as variations in the center of gravity and the moment of inertia. In this way, the leveling torque does not explicitly appear in the dynamic model.
The final experimental results show that the method proposed in this paper reduces the control error (RMSE) by \textbf{45.3\%}.
Please check the supplementary material at:
\url{https://github.com/ZJU-FAST-Lab/Ground-effect-controller}.



\end{abstract}


\begin{IEEEkeywords}
    Ground effect, multicopter control, disturbance modeling.
\end{IEEEkeywords}



\section{Introduction}
\label{sec:intro}



% 由于简单的机械设计和高机动性，多旋翼飞行器广泛应用于开阔天空和狭窄的室内环境。然而，在许多应用中，难以避免地需要进行近地操作。
% 例如，使用带有机械臂的无人机靠近地面抓取物体，规划近地面飞行的轨迹来利用地面效应提供的额外推力节省能量，自动降落到物体表面。
% 在这些场景中，当飞行器接近刚性结构时，受到地面或物体表面附近气流的干扰，这明显影响了安全性和稳定性。
% 图1展示了无人机在地面附近飞行时的情况，其中图1b中可以看出无人机的气流在地面影响下发生了大幅度变化。

\IEEEPARstart{T}hanks to the simple mechanical design and high maneuverability,
multicopters are widely used in both open sky and indoor environments.
However, near-ground operations are unavoidable in many applications.
For example, using a multicopter with an arm to grab an object close to the ground\cite{fishman2021dynamic, saunders2024autonomous}, planning a near-ground trajectory to use the extra thrust provided by ground effect to save energy\cite{gao2019exploiting}, flying in the tunnel \cite{wang2022neither} or along the wall \cite{ding2022passive} automatically landing on the surface of the object\cite{luo2015biomimetic, ji2022real}, and so on.
In these scenarios, when approaching rigid structures, multicopters are disturbed by the airflow near surfaces of ground or objects, which significantly influences the safety and stability.
Fig.~\ref{fig_head}(a) illustrates the scenario of a multicopter flying close to the ground.
In Fig.~\ref{fig_head}(b), it is evident that the airflow around the multicopter changes significantly under the influence of the ground.




\begin{figure}[t]
