\subsubsection{Mathematical explanations}

% 我们将尝试做一些数学推导来解释这些猜想和仿真的结果。

We conduct some mathematical derivations to explain these assumptions and simulation results.


% 假设地面效应力f分布在以机体中心为圆心，对角轴距b为直径的一个圆上。这个圆心离地高度为h，圆上的点离地高度为H。圆上的离地最低点a=0。D是地面效应力f在圆上的分布密度函数。我们可以得到：


Assuming the additional force ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ by ground effect is distributed on a circle with the quadrotor's center as its center and the diagonal wheelbase $b$ as its diameter.
The center of this circle is located at a height $h$ above the ground, and the height of the points on the circle is $H\left( \theta  \right)\left\{ {\theta  \in \left[ {0,2\pi } \right)} \right\}$.
The point closest to the ground corresponds to $\theta {\rm{ = }}0$.
${D\left( \theta  \right)}$ represents the distribution density function of the ground effect force ${{\bm{\tau }}_{\bm{G}}}$ on the circle. The relationship can be expressed as follows:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_getorque_model}
    \int_0^{2\pi } {D\left( \theta  \right)d\theta = {F_G}\left( h \right)T} \\
    D\left( \theta  \right) = {F_G}\left[ {H\left( \theta  \right)} \right]T/2\pi \\
    H\left( \theta  \right) = h - \frac{b}{2}\sin \delta \cos \theta ,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $\delta$ is the angle between the Z-axis of the body system and the world coordinate system.



We assume that around a certain height, $ {\dot F_G}\left( h \right) $ is a constant value:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_Fgh_diff}
    {F_G}\left[ {H\left( \theta  \right)} \right]{\rm{ = }}{F_G}\left( h \right) - \frac{b}{2}\sin \delta \cos \theta {\dot F_G} \left( h \right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The torque $\left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right|$ is created by the $\left| {{{\bm{f}}_G}} \right|$ distributed on the circle:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_getorque_norm}
    \left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right| & = \int_0^{2\pi } {D\left( \theta  \right)\frac{b}{2}\cos \theta d\theta } \\
    & = \frac{{bT}}{{2\pi }}\int_0^\pi  {\left[ {{F_G}\left( h \right) - \frac{b}{2}\sin \delta \cos \theta {\dot F_G} \left( h \right)} \right]\cos \theta d\theta } \\
    & =  - \frac{1}{8}{b^2}\sin \delta {\dot F_G} \left( h \right)T.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}




The vector form of ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ in the body coordinate system can be written as
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_getorque_vec}
    {\bf{R}}{{\bm{\tau }}_G} = \left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right|\left( {{{\bf{z}}_B} \times {{\bf{z}}_W}} \right) = {M_G}\left( h \right)T\left( {{{\bf{z}}_B} \times {{\bf{z}}_W}} \right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
${M_G}\left( h \right)$ can be regarded as

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_Mh}
    {M_G}\left( h \right) = \frac{{{g_5}h}}{{{{\left( {{h^2} + {g_3}h + {g_4}} \right)}^2}}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}



\subsubsection{Calibrate parameters with the real-world platform}

% 我们需要通过实际的实验来验证上述的模型并标定参数，用于实际的无人机控制。

We need to validate the above model and calibrate parameters through real-world experiments.


% 如图1的平台所示，我们将四旋翼固定在测力支架上，调节玻纤板倾角和离地高度。推动油门并保持4个桨叶转速一致。采集倾角、离地高度、转速和力传感器数据。

As shown in Fig.~\ref{fig_model_valid}(e$\sim$g), on the quadrotor platform, we adjust the tilt angle of the ground board and the height of the quadrotor, increase throttle and maintain consistent speeds for all four rotors. Data on tilt angle, height, rotor speeds, and torques are collected.

% 从表1中可以看出，外力矩A有和高度、转速\倾角强相关。
From Fig.~\ref{fit_getorque_rpm} and Fig.\ref{getorque_combine} (more data in MAT.Part.4.2 \cite{groundeffectgithub}),
it is evident that ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ exhibits a strong correlation with both altitude $h$, tilt angle, and average rotor speed.



\begin{itemize}
\item ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ and $ T $: 
    % 图1展示了在四旋翼平台上，不同倾角和高度下，地面效应扭矩M与平均转速的关系。
    % 可以看出在不同的的倾角和高度下，扭矩都和转速的平方（也可以说是推力）成正比。由公式1，可以认为在一定倾角和高度下,地面效应扭矩M与推力T正比。
    Fig.~\ref{fit_getorque_rpm} illustrates the relationship between leveling torque ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ and average rotational speed $\left\| {{n_i}} \right\|$ under varying heights on the quadrotor platform.
    It is evident that, there is a proportional relationship between the leveling torque and the square of the average rotation speed (or thrust according to (\ref{equ_rpm_to_thrust})):

    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
    \label{equ_torque_rpm}
        \left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right| \sim {\left\| {{n_i}} \right\|^2} \sim T.
    \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}



\item ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ and $ \delta  $: 
    % 如图2b所示，水平力矩外力矩基本和倾角成正比。但是当倾角较大时（大于10度），水平力矩不会继续增加。
    As shown in Fig.~\ref{getorque_combine}b, the leveling torque is proportional to the tilt angle:
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
    \label{equ_torque_angle}
        \left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right|\sim \delta \left( {\delta  \to 0} \right).
    \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}

    However, as the tilt angle becomes larger ($\delta  > 10{\rm{^\circ }}$), the leveling torque ceases to increase.


\item ${{\bm{\tau }}_G}$ and $ h $: 
    % 从图2可以看出，倾角固定，无人机高度高度逐渐降低时，地面效应扭矩的绝对值先增大后减小，和仿真的结果（图1）趋势一致。这验证了之前的猜想，也标定了公式1的参数。
    From Fig.~\ref{getorque_combine}(a), it can be observed that, under a fixed tilt angle, as the quadrotor's altitude gradually decreases, the leveling torque initially increases and then decreases.
    This validates our previous assumption in Sec.~\ref{subsubsec:assumption} and also calibrates the parameters of (\ref{equ_Mh}).

\end{itemize}


% 我们得到了这样一个重要的结论，我们后续也将通过实物实验验证：随着高度降低，水平力矩的绝对值，在距离地面一定距离会达到峰值，然后逐渐下降，而不是单调的上升。

\noindent
\textbf{\emph{Conclusion 1:}}

\textbf{As the height decreases, the absolute value of the leveling torque $\left| {{{\bm{\tau }}_G}} \right|$ reaches a maximum at a certain distance from the ground, then gradually decreases, rather than monotonically increasing.}



