\subsection{Other Outputs}
\label{subsec:flat_other}

% 我们可以通过对公式1多次求导来获得角速度和角加速度的参考输出，具体的推导过程与论文1类似。在求导过程中，由于无人机在执行近地飞行轨迹时一般不会有很大的Z轴速度，因此可以认为：

We can obtain the reference outputs of angular velocity $ {{\bm{\omega }}_{ref}} $ and angular acceleration $ {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{ref}} $ by differentiating the acceleration in (\ref{equ_flat_model})
The detailed derivation process is similar to the previous works \cite{faessler2017differential, wang2022geometrically}.
In the differentiation process, since the multicopter generally does not have a significant Z-axis velocity when executing a near-ground flight trajectory, we can assume that
$ \frac{d}{{dt}}D\left( h \right) = \frac{{{d^2}}}{{d{t^2}}}D\left( h \right) = 0 $.


Then the reference torque input can be obtained:


\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_flat_torque}
    {{\bm{\tau }}_{ref}} = {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right){{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{ref}} + {{\bm{\omega }}_{ref}} \times {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right){{\bm{\omega }}_{ref}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

% 其中j'(h)使用了公式1的结论，体现了高度对转动惯量模型的影响
${\bm{J}'}\left( h \right)$ uses the conclusion from (\ref{equ_ge_interia_adjust})(\ref{equ_MGT}), illustrating the effect of leveling torque model on the differential flatness.


\section{Model-based Controller with Incremental Inversion}
\label{sec:controller}


% 这一部分将利用前文的模型，对外力加速度和外力矩进行补偿，从而对近地面飞行的无人机进行控制。最重要的对水平力矩的补偿在sec1中。

This section will use the previously introduced model to compensate for external disturbances, thereby controlling the quadrotor during near-ground flight.
The most important part is the compensation of the leveling torque in Sec.~\ref{subsec:thrust_torque}.



\subsection{Acceleration Command}
\label{subsec:acccmd}


% 通常，补偿无人机受到的外力有两种方式。
% 第一种是通过外力观测器，将合外力加速度加到控制回路中。这种方式可以不依赖模型，但是估计存在延迟和噪声，可能对控制造成影响。
% 第二种是预测期望状态会受到的外力，并将其作为前馈补偿。这种情况下外力模型需要是确定的。
% Generally, there are two ways to compensate for external forces acting on the multicopter.
% \begin{itemize}
%     \item
%     Using an external force observer to introduce the resultant external acceleration into the control loop, which is called the \emph{dynamic inversion},
%     This approach does not rely on the accurate model but may suffer from delays and noises of the external force estimation.
%     \item
%     Predicting the external forces at the desired state use them as feedforward compensation, which needs accurate calibrated dynamic model.
% \end{itemize}



% 考虑到我们已经建立了精确的外力模型，为了避免噪声和控制误差，我们依赖推力和阻力模型来进行补偿。

Given that we establish an accurate external force model, we rely on these models to compensate disturbances to reduce control errors.
% 期望合加速度为
The expected resultant acceleration is
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_total_acc}
    {{\bm{a}}_{des}} & = {{\bm{a}}_{ref}} + {{\bm{a}}_E} - {{\bm{a}}_D} - {{\bm{a}}_G}, \\
    {{\bm{a}}_E} & = {{\bm{K}}^P}\left( {{{\bm{p}}_{des}} - {\bm{\hat p}}} \right) + {{\bm{K}}^V}\left( {{{\bm{v}}_{des}} - {\bm{\hat v}}} \right), \\
    {{\bm{a}}_D} & =  - {\bm{R}}\frac{{{\bm{D}}\left( h \right)}}{m}{{\bm{R}}^ \top }{{\bm{v}}_{ref}}, \\
    {{\bm{a}}_G} & = \frac{{{T_{ref}}}}{m}{F_G}\left( h \right){{\bm{z}}_B}.    
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
% 其中aref是运动轨迹上的参考加速度
% 其中ae是由位置和速度误差反馈产生的加速度
${{\bm{a}}_{ref}} $ represents the reference acceleration (\ref{equ_flatness}) along the motion trajectory, 
${{\bm{a}}_E}$ is the acceleration resulting from the position and velocity error feedback, 
(${\bm{K}}^P$ and ${\bm{K}}^V$ are the parameters of the PD controller for position control.),
${{\bm{a}}_D}$ and ${{\bm{a}}_G}$ are the accelerations from the drag (\ref{equ_ge_drag_h}) and additional thrust model(\ref{equ_geforce}) respectively.

\subsection{Attitude, Bodyrate and Body Acceleration Command}

% 我们可以通过微分平坦关系由期望加速度得到期望姿态：
We can get the desired attitude from the desired acceleration using the principles of differential flatness in Sec.~\ref{sec:flatness}:

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_q_cmd}
    {{\bm{a}}_{des}} \leftrightarrow {{\bm{\xi }}_{des}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

% 当前姿态与期望姿态的误差为：我们可以通过当前姿态和期望姿态的四元数，得到一个姿态的误差：
The error between the current attitude ${{\bm{\hat \xi }}}$ and the expected attitude ${{\bm{\xi }}_{des}}$ is:

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_quat_qerror}
    {{\bm{\xi }}_e} = {\bm{\hat \xi }} \circ {{\bm{\xi }}_{des}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The attitudes here are all quaternion forms. The $ \circ $ means the Hamilton quaternion product.
%将其写为angle vector的形式：
Write it into an angle vector:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_angle_qerror}
    {{\bm{\xi }}_e}' = \frac{{2{{\cos }^{ - 1}}{\bm{\xi }}_{e}^w}}{{\sqrt {1 - {\bm{\xi }}{{_{e}^w}^2}} }}{\left[ {\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}
    {{\bm{\xi }}_{e}^x}&{{\bm{\xi }}_{e}^y}&{{\bm{\xi }}_{e}^z}
    \end{array}} \right]^ \top },
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $\left[ {\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}
    {{{\bm{\xi }}^w}}&{{{\bm{\xi }}^x}}&{{{\bm{\xi }}^y}}&{{{\bm{\xi }}^z}}
    \end{array}} \right]$
is the quaternion form of the attitude.
% 接下来可以计算出期望的角速度和角加速度。其中K1、K2是角度控制的PD参数，w1、w2分别是通过EQU1得到的参考角速度和角加速度。
Subsequently, we can calculate the desired angular velocity and angular acceleration:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_bodyrate_cmd}
    {{\bm{\omega }}_{des}} & = {{\bm{K}}^{\bm{\xi }}}{{\bm{\xi }}_e}' + {{\bm{\omega }}_{ref}} \\
    {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} & = {{\bm{K}}^\omega }\left( {{{\bm{\omega }}_{des}} - {{\bm{\omega }}_f}} \right) + {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{ref}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
In this context, $ {{\bm{K}}^{\bm{\xi }}} $ and $ {{\bm{K}}^\omega } $ are the PD parameters for angle control, and $ {{\bm{\omega }}_{ref}} $, $ {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{ref}} $  are the reference angular velocity and angular acceleration derived from (\ref{equ_flatness}) respectively.



\subsection{Thrust and Torque Command}
\label{subsec:thrust_torque}
% 期望加速度在无人机z轴方向上的投影即为电机需要产生的加速度，由此可以得到期望推力：
The desired acceleration projected onto the quadrotor's Z-axis corresponds to the acceleration the rotors need to produce. Then we can get the expected thrust:


\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_acc_cmd}
    {T_{des}} = m{{\bm{a}}_{des}}\frac{{{{{\bm{\hat z}}}_B}}}{{\left| {{{{\bm{\hat z}}}_B}} \right|}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

% 通过期望角速度和期望角加速度可以计算电机需要产生的力矩，和高度相关的转动惯量Jh可以补偿由于地面效应带来的力矩影响
The torque required from the motors can be calculated based on the desired angular velocity and desired angular acceleration:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_torque_cmd}
    {}^B{{\bm{\tau }}_{des}} = {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) \cdot {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} + {{\bm{\omega }}_{des}} \times {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) \cdot {{\bm{\omega }}_{des}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The rotational inertia $ {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) $, which is altitude-dependent, serves to compensate for the torque effects induced by ground effect.



% 由于多方面的原因，上述的方法并不能完全抵消外力矩的影响。第一是基于测力支架得到的参数不完全准确，第二是无人机还存在其他未建模的力矩，例如重心偏移、陀螺力矩等。为此，我们结合了INDI的方法来进行输出控制力矩：


Due to various reasons, the above method cannot completely compensate for the external torques.
Firstly, the parameters obtained based on the torque measurement platform are not entirely accurate.
Secondly, there are other unmodeled torques, such as the gravity torque and the gyroscopic torque.
Therefore, we combine the incremental nonlinear dynamic inversion \cite{tal2020accurate} with our model to output the control torque:

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_torque_cmd_indi}
    {}^B{{\bm{\tau }}_{des}} = {{{\bm{\hat \tau }}}_B} + {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) \cdot \left( {{{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} - {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_f}} \right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}



% 这里随高度变化的转动惯量有2种理解。
% 第一是地面效应水平力矩快速变化，如果直接用传统的INDI方法，补偿的力矩的绝对值是偏小的。
% 第二种是，对实时估计的外力矩进行补偿，本质上是将角加速度误差AAA引入了反馈，但是其误差增益是固定的转动惯量J。如果J是可调的，那意味着角加速度增益的调节也更自由，可以适应场景的变化。

% There are two explanations for the altitude-varying of inertia moment $ {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) $ in the control method:
% \begin{itemize}
% \item
%     The leveling torque change rapidly. If we directly apply the traditional INDI method, the compensation for the torque is not strong enough:

%     \begin{equation}
%     \begin{aligned}
%     \label{equ_indicomp}
%         \left| {{\bm{J}} \cdot \left( {{{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} - {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_f}} \right)} \right| < \left| {{\bm{J}}'\left( h \right) \cdot \left( {{{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} - {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_f}} \right)} \right|.
%     \end{aligned}
%     \end{equation}


% \item
%     Compensation for the external torque by real-time estimation essentially introduces feedback for angular acceleration error $ {\left( {{{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_{des}} - {{{\bm{\dot \omega }}}_f}} \right)} $, where the gain is the fixed inertia moment of $ \bm{J} $.
%     If $ \bm{J} $ is adjustable, it means that the angular acceleration error gain is flexible and can adapt to changes in flight conditions.

% \end{itemize}




% 实际上，我们在实验过程中，依然需要对J(h)函数进行微调。这种基于模型的补偿方法，也就退化为了对角加速度误差反馈增益系数的调节。
% 这使得我们的方法在具有科学解释的同时，也具备了工程上的价值：即可以依据实际飞行情况进行调参，而不是必须严格的依靠参数标定平台

% In practice, we still need to fine-tune the function $ {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) $ during the experiment.
% The model-based compensation method then degrades to adjust the gain of the angular acceleration error.
% This gives our approach an engineering value as well as a scientific explanation: parameters can be adjusted based on actual flight conditions, rather than having to rely on a parameter calibration platform strictly.

% 实际上，我们在实验过程中，依然需要对J(h)函数进行微调。
% 这种基于模型的补偿方法，也就退化为了对角加速度误差反馈增益系数的调节。

In practice, we still need to fine-tune the function $ {\bm{J}'}\left( h \right) $ during the experiment.
The model-based compensation method then degrades to adjust the gain of the angular acceleration error.
% 这种做法，等效于将常规旋翼无人机的双环姿态控制器中的角速度控制增益，设定为一个和高度有关的函数，也类似于分段式PID，在工程上具备较高的可行性。
This approach is equivalent to setting the angular velocity control gain in a conventional dual-loop attitude controller as a height-dependent function. It is also similar to a \textit{piecewise PID controller}, making it highly feasible for engineering applications.



\subsection{Rotor Speed Command}

% 根据公式1的混控矩阵的逆，可以由推力和扭矩计算出每个电机的转速：
Based on the inverse of the mixed control matrix in (\ref{equ_mixmatrix}), the rotational speeds of each motor can be computed from the thrust and torques:


\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{equ_rpm_cmd}
    {{\bm{N}}_{des}}^2 = {M^{ - 1}}\left[ {\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}
    {{T_{des}}}\\
    {{}^B{{\bm{\tau }}_{des}}}
    \end{array}} \right].
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}




% 电机转速可以通过发送的油门控制，转速通过BDSHOT回传。
% 电机建模、标定和转速控制的方式在附录中介绍。

The rotor speeds are controlled through the throttle input ($t_i^{des} \in \left[ {0,1} \right]$), and the rotational speeds are fed back through \emph{BDhot}.
Methods of motor modeling \cite{brandt2011propeller,zhang2022visual}, calibration and speed control are described in MAT.Part.3 \cite{groundeffectgithub}.

% 我们修改了APM固件的部分代码以适配油门接口和电压补偿逻辑。我们后续将开源这一版本的固件代码。
We refine the code of the APM firmware \cite{groundeffectgithub}
to align with the throttle interface and voltage compensation logic, which has been open-sourced \cite{groundeffectgithub}.






