The increasing complexity of semiconductor technology and the number of required PVT corners have introduced severe challenges in CCS characterization due to the high accuracy requirement, large volume of data, and extensive simulation overhead \cite{siemens}.
First, capturing detailed current waveforms requires high-precision measurements and simulations to accurately reflect the dynamic behavior of the driver during switching. 
