Context-free grammars are the fundamental way to specify the syntactic space of a programming language, and with the grammar specified, a program can be parsed into a syntax tree, revealing its structure~\cite{compiler}. Building on this foundation, leveraging grammatical knowledge~(e.g., grammar rules) to pre-train large language models~(LLMs) has emerged as a promising strategy for code-related tasks, such as code generation~\cite{grammart5, treegen, graphcodebert2020}.

