\Description{}
\end{figure}

The key processing stages in the Doom environment are illustrated in Fig. \ref{fig:doom}: image resizing, 1x1 convolution, color quantization, and attention ($k=1$). Remarkably, the evolved agent adopts a surprisingly minimalist strategy, ignoring seemingly critical elements like incoming fireballs. Instead, it focuses exclusively on the rightmost monster on screen while executing a rhythmic left-to-right movement pattern. This strategy matches the performance of the patch-based model, despite the latter attending to both fireballs and walls. The equivalence to our simple approach suggests that the patch-based model's LSTM might also be relying primarily on periodic movement and ignoring projectile coordinates. This strategy proves effective because the monsters' projectiles target the agent's current position -- continuous movement therefore serves as a robust avoidance technique, regardless of the specific locations of incoming fire. However, our $k=10$ agent seems more reactive to fireballs.

