%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Conclusion}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

Our approach provides pixel-precise generative image editing in intrinsic space. It is made possible by \xrgb diffusion inversion, optimizing both the noise and the prompt embedding to flexibly preserve non-edited information from the input image. We show the capabilities of our framework on a diverse set of non-trivial image manipulation tasks, including object insertion and removal, material editing, and full scene relighting. Despite some remaining limitations, our results demonstrate substantial progress towards unlocking the potential of generative decompose-edit-recompose approaches for image editing.


