In (a), relying on a virtual voxel center can lead to projection errors, which become more pronounced for larger voxels and cause mismatches between LiDAR and image data. This motivates the use of physical points.
In (b), canonical PE (row 1) overlooks the varying sizes of voxel and image features, while focusing solely on the region of physical points (row 2) limits the receptive field. Hence, we introduce a \textbf{scale-aware PE} that uses extreme points, as shown in \tb{(c)}.
}
\vspace{-2em}
