The first tutorial covered the basics of logic modeling with Z3 in the SMTLIB format following parts of the SMTLIB Tutorial in \tool (\autoref{fig:smtlib}) and the formula guessing games (\autoref{fig:secret-formula}), while the second introduced using the Z3 solver API in JavaScript and Python for solving realistic constraint-satisfaction problems (e.g., \autoref{fig:js}).
