As shown in Table~\ref{label_3}, as the missing rate increases, the F1 score and accuracy (ACC) of all methods decrease. However, our method demonstrates superior stability, with the smallest performance drop and minimal fluctuation even at higher missing rates.
This stability is attributed to the decoupling of the feature extraction network in our model, which effectively mitigates the impact of missing modalities on the overall model's performance.


