$\rho^*=2.07$, (innermost cell, green) and refined Q cell $Q^*(\rho)$ (blue boundary),
and the simulated boundary of the second-order cell $Q^{(2)}$ (red line). The
corners of $Q(\rho^*)$, marked with red crosses, lie on the boundary of $Q^{(2)}$.
The black line segments mark the boundaries of the half-planes touching the corners of $Q(\rho^*)$, effectively
``cutting the corners" off of $Q(\rho)$. In this example, the refined Q cell is 8\% smaller than the original Q cell.}
