\textbf{Quality percentile guarantee:} A defining feature of real-time video is that each packet must be delivered within a specific deadline; otherwise, the packet loses its value or becomes significantly less useful. 
For real-time traffic, timely delivery (i.e., delivery within deadline) of packets plays a critical role in determining user experience.  The quality of experience (QoE) for users is highly dependent on timely delivery, as excessive delays lead to video freezing, stalling, or degradation in video quality. 

