A typical prompt comprises three primary components, as shown in Figure~\ref{fig: Components of LLM Prompt}.


\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item Instruction: Explicitly defines the task the model is expected to perform, such as summarizing text, translating languages, or classifying sentiments.
    \item Context or Examples: Provides additional context or illustrative examples (often referred to as "few-shot examples") to clearly indicate the desired behavior or response pattern.
    \item Input or Query: Presents the specific question or input requiring a response from the model.
\end{enumerate}	
Consider the following structured example:

