too discriminating to be useful in practice. We want to contradict this opinion by means of the simple case study in Figure \ref{upc1-place},
which shows two forms of optimization which do not
alter the essential behavior of the system. We refer in
particular to replication (exemplified by transition {\em del}) and unfolding (exemplified by transition {\em prod}).

